Here are a few thoughts about making pools usefull and entertaining :

I think NetHack should have a bit more water folklore than it has.
Right now, NetHack has only water potions, sinks, fountains, pools and
moats. Where as rock has a whole range of monsters, tools, and properties.

Ok, now for the raw, unsorted random ideas:

2 types of pools :
   a) Puddles (shallow pools) : created by the overflowing of fountains
      and who knows, maybe some blobs or jellies?
      Maybe, fountains should overflow randomly (not systematic diagonals)
      They act as slippery traps : if you fail some dexterity check, you
      slip. Chance of stunning (short), chance of breaking potions in
      backpack.
   b) Pool (deep pools) : It is a water filled pit. If a fountain overflows
      every pit in the room fills with water. Can be viewed as a one square
      moat. But don't fill staircases leading down (maybe wash small objects
      down to the next floor.)

How should pools be handled ? My suggestion :
I'll ignore the confirmation thing and assume no confirm for now.

Hebrais the Stripling is walking along and steps on a pool.

You fall in a pool! You sink right to the bottom --more--
              (sees himself as in a vortex)
You see here 37 zorkmids --more-- (the bait)

at this point, he has 2 round to get out.

<Drop> <all> (I'm assuming he has no metal armor. But robes, boots, gloves,
              hats should be all right)
You can't keep your breath any longer --more--
<Up>
You make it to the surface --more--

if you are light enough, you can swim (udhjklyubn).
All scrolls are obviously blanked. Unless they are in a scroll case (a form
of small waterproof box. You could only store scrolls in it.

Consequences of going underwater :
     *  Some way to breathe : ring, spell and intrinsic water breathing.
              You could get intrinsic from eating any amphibian (new monster?)
              (Someone suggested earlier that a cursed ring of water breathing
               Would let you only breathe water. I like the idea ;-)
     *  Unless you have some item (helm of underwater action?), you are slowed.
        But monsters (native to the water element) would not be so.
     *  Scrolls and spell books are blanked (as stated previously).
               Even if you protect them, you should not be able to use them.
     *  Potions have no effect (you can't drink from a bottle underwater,
               the best you can do is dilute the potion)

Item ideas :
     *  ring of waterbreathing
     *  boot of underwater action (rubber boots in unidentified, noisy if
        on dry ground). Counteracts the slow effect.
     *  tridents as a weapon
        Including a named one. Can't think of an appropriate name.

Monsters you could encounter in moats and on special level:
     +  Eye of the Deep (floating eye in disguise)
     -  The whole range of slimes, blobs and jellies.
     -  Water nymph
     -  Water elemental (invisible)
     +  Pyrannas (similar to bees)
     -  Crocodiles
     -  Eels
     +  Electric eels.
     -  Kraken
     !  And many more
I believe there is almost enough water monsters to make one level of it in the
current version.

Now, my special levels (actual numbers not relevant):
Level 12: The Siren's level
Level 13: The Aquarium

On the Siren's level (Does the little siren in Copenhagen have a name?),
you'll find a room that looks like that:

    +---@---+
    |..}}}..|
    |.......|
    |..}...@-
    |......d|
    |.....}F|
    +---.---+

Since you got on this level, you've been hearing pieces of harp playing and
soft singing. Also, there is an unusual number of pools, puddles fountains,
blobs, jellies and other amphibian nasties. If you actually go in the Sirens
room, her singing might charm you and you'll blindlessly run to her, fall in
the pool and she'll jump in after you attacking wildly. (Note that this
pool is 3 squares big and the 'underwater map' should reflect that).

You will not find a stair case down in this level, it is submerged!
One of the pools has no bottom and leads to the water level.

Note that water breathing should be gained easily by eathing some monster
on this level.

To get out of the water level, you'll have to operate the sas:
a 2X2 room with 2 doors, no matter what, you can't open both doors at the
same time. The second door leads to another small room with a stair case
down.
The water level is full of giant oyster, real tough to crack open but they
are defenseless and contain a perl. (Maybe a can opener can help ;-)

Well, that's enough bandwidth wasted for one night.
I'd just like to mention I don't like some of the ideas I've presented,
in particular, I don't really want to see another map style. Just
more monster, items, intrinsics, folklore etc...

PS: Most of these ideas are not original, please forgive me for
not including due credit.

Disclamer : I'm VERY satisfied with the program as it is. I was just
dreaming and thought some of you'd like to read about my dreams ;-)
